{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg72X7i9K2rNqFa23YLZJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest stable React is **19.3.1**, according to the npm registry (`latest` dist-tag). A 19.3 canary is also published, and its most recent build is dated 2026-10-15.\n\nMy web search only turned up pages that listed 19.2 as the latest, from the October 2025 release post, so those pages are out of date. I trust the npm result over them.\n\n- **Security fixes:** In December 2025, a critical React Server Components vulnerability was fixed in 19.0.1, 19.1.2 and 19.2.1. Any version at or above 19.2.1 includes that fix, and so does 19.3.1.\n- **What changed in 19.3:** I didn't find a release post for 19.3. Check [react.dev/blog](https://react.dev/blog) or the GitHub changelog before upgrading.\n\nTo upgrade, run `npm i react@latest react-dom@latest`.\n\nSources:\n- [React Versions](https://zh-hant.react.dev/versions)\n- [React Blog](https://react.dev/blog)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":19469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"output_tokens":336,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3b000d9-dc41-4ef1-8992-335e348d4817","uuid":"5ec27025-8bba-4d42-b0ad-84156a17eb28","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:33:25.139Z","request_id":"req_011Cg72X7V1KkS4idmrmVtwa"}
